{"explanation":"Encryption now supplies a fresh 96-bit nonce and explicit 128-bit GCM authentication-tag parameters while preserving the existing public encrypt/decrypt signatures, AES/GCM/NoPadding transformation, AAD binding, stored AlgorithmParameters encoding, and decryption of self-contained existing records. The provider-specific GCMParameterSpec and AlgorithmParameters behavior requires manual Android-provider validation before publication.","review_assumptions":["The Android API levels and installed AES/GCM provider support javax.crypto.spec.GCMParameterSpec with a 96-bit nonce and 128-bit tag length.","After initialization from GCMParameterSpec, the active provider returns non-null, encoded AlgorithmParameters that can be reconstructed by the existing decrypt path for both newly written and legacy records.","The required provenance review for keys supplied by MasterKey and Encryptor is performed independently; this edit intentionally does not alter caller-supplied key provenance."],"no_change_required":false,"decision":"MULTI_FILE_FIX_PROPOSED_FOR_REVIEW","confidence":"medium","edits":[{"source_file_path":"mobile/src/main/java/org/fedorahosted/freeotp/encryptor/EncryptedKey.java","original_code":"import java.security.NoSuchAlgorithmException;
","edit_kind":"declaration","corrected_code":"import java.security.NoSuchAlgorithmException;
import java.security.SecureRandom;
","reason":"Import the cryptographically secure random source used to create a distinct GCM nonce for each encryption.","symbol":"EncryptedKey imports"},{"source_file_path":"mobile/src/main/java/org/fedorahosted/freeotp/encryptor/EncryptedKey.java","original_code":"import javax.crypto.SecretKey;
import javax.crypto.spec.SecretKeySpec;
","edit_kind":"declaration","corrected_code":"import javax.crypto.SecretKey;
import javax.crypto.spec.GCMParameterSpec;
import javax.crypto.spec.SecretKeySpec;
","reason":"Import the explicit GCM parameter specification used when initializing encryption.","symbol":"EncryptedKey imports"},{"source_file_path":"mobile/src/main/java/org/fedorahosted/freeotp/encryptor/EncryptedKey.java","original_code":"    private final byte[] mCipherText;
    private final byte[] mParameters;
    private final String mCipher;
    private final String mToken;
","edit_kind":"declaration","corrected_code":"    private static final int GCM_TAG_LENGTH_BITS = 128;
    private static final int GCM_NONCE_LENGTH_BYTES = 12;
    private static final SecureRandom SECURE_RANDOM = new SecureRandom();

    private final byte[] mCipherText;
    private final byte[] mParameters;
    private final String mCipher;
    private final String mToken;
","reason":"Define the standard 96-bit GCM nonce length and 128-bit authentication tag length, with one reusable cryptographically secure random source for nonce generation.","symbol":"EncryptedKey GCM parameters"},{"source_file_path":"mobile/src/main/java/org/fedorahosted/freeotp/encryptor/EncryptedKey.java","original_code":"    public static EncryptedKey encrypt(SecretKey key, SecretKey plaintext)
            throws NoSuchAlgorithmException, NoSuchPaddingException, InvalidKeyException,
            BadPaddingException, IllegalBlockSizeException, IOException {
        if (key == null) {
            throw new InvalidKeyException("Key is null");
        }
        Cipher cipher = Cipher.getInstance("AES/GCM/NoPadding");
        cipher.init(Cipher.ENCRYPT_MODE, key);
        return new EncryptedKey(cipher, plaintext);
    }
","edit_kind":"method","corrected_code":"    public static EncryptedKey encrypt(SecretKey key, SecretKey plaintext)
            throws NoSuchAlgorithmException, NoSuchPaddingException, InvalidKeyException,
            BadPaddingException, IllegalBlockSizeException, IOException {
        if (key == null) {
            throw new InvalidKeyException("Key is null");
        }

        byte[] nonce = new byte[GCM_NONCE_LENGTH_BYTES];
        SECURE_RANDOM.nextBytes(nonce);

        Cipher cipher = Cipher.getInstance("AES/GCM/NoPadding");
        try {
            cipher.init(Cipher.ENCRYPT_MODE, key,
                    new GCMParameterSpec(GCM_TAG_LENGTH_BITS, nonce));
        } catch (InvalidAlgorithmParameterException e) {
            throw new IllegalStateException("Provider rejected explicit GCM parameters", e);
        }
        return new EncryptedKey(cipher, plaintext);
    }
","reason":"Initialize AES/GCM encryption from freshly generated explicit nonce and tag parameters rather than relying on the provider's two-argument initialization. The existing constructor continues to bind the plaintext-key algorithm as AAD and persist the resulting AlgorithmParameters; the public checked-exception signature remains unchanged and provider rejection is propagated with its cause.","symbol":"EncryptedKey.encrypt"}],"manual_review_required":true,"provided_contracts":["EncryptedKey.encrypt retains its existing public signature and AES/GCM/NoPadding transformation.","Each new encryption initializes GCM with a freshly generated 96-bit nonce and a 128-bit authentication tag specification.","EncryptedKey continues to persist provider-produced AlgorithmParameters, ciphertext, cipher transformation, and AAD selector data; decrypt remains unchanged and reconstructs stored AlgorithmParameters."],"required_contracts":["MasterKey and Encryptor key-provenance changes, if warranted by the required CrySL trace, must preserve EncryptedKey.encrypt(SecretKey, SecretKey) as the caller entry point.","Instrumentation tests must verify round-trip decryption, serialized-record compatibility including a legacy fixture, and distinct GCM parameters/nonces for repeated encryption under one key.","Android-provider review must confirm explicit GCMParameterSpec initialization and subsequent AlgorithmParameters encoding/decoding work on supported API levels."],"source_file_path":"mobile/src/main/java/org/fedorahosted/freeotp/encryptor/EncryptedKey.java","required_tests":["Edit mobile/src/androidTest/java/org/fedorahosted/freeotp/EncryptedKeyTest.java to cover encrypt/decrypt round trips for every production key path selected by the provenance review.","Edit mobile/src/androidTest/java/org/fedorahosted/freeotp/EncryptedKeyTest.java to verify decryption of serialized records retaining cipher algorithm, AlgorithmParameters, ciphertext, and plaintext-key-algorithm/AAD-selector fields, including a pre-change record fixture or equivalent legacy record.","Edit mobile/src/androidTest/java/org/fedorahosted/freeotp/EncryptedKeyTest.java to verify that repeated encryptions using one key use separately prepared GCM parameters/nonces and decrypt successfully after serialization."]}
